{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets (excl. territories) and the 2025 population from the census file's own 'United States' row : how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786911837572},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Get total farmers markets (excluding territories) from the first CSV\n2. Get 2025 population from the second CSV's \"United States\" row\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents to 4 decimal places\n4. Return as one confident sentence\n5. Use tools for any math\n\nLet me start by understanding the catalog situation. I should check if there's already a catalog with these sources, or if I need to ingest them.\n\nFirst, let me follow the procedure:\n1. Orient - check for semantic models and existing aliases\n2. Compute values from the catalog\n3. Declare obligations and verify\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by orienting to the catalog and then ingest these data sources."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KJ4XtCsqTpNDDSL4KUn3QY","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01PbhXMXQphGCJoyLrE34UUS","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":310,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8177,"totalTokens":8497,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0015500000000000002,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01022125,"total":0.01178125},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":160},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786911837584,"responseId":"msg_011Ce741SvjrSW4ApPBaETuJ","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01KJ4XtCsqTpNDDSL4KUn3QY","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786911842393},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01PbhXMXQphGCJoyLrE34UUS","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786911842393},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both CSV sources. Let me create build scripts for both datasets. I'll need to:\n\n1. Create a script to read the farmers markets CSV and count markets excluding territories\n2. Create a script to read the census CSV and extract US population for 2025\n3. Then create a script that combines these to calculate the ratio\n\nLet me start by creating the build scripts in .xorq/scripts/","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The catalog is empty, so I'll ingest both data sources. Let me create build scripts for each dataset."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_016f2N94MnGiwMqJWPgGLUg5","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p .xorq/scripts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":188,"cacheRead":8177,"cacheWrite":407,"totalTokens":8786,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0009400000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0008177000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00050875,"total":0.0022804500000000003},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":102},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786911842394,"responseId":"msg_011Ce741oBek2T2WabBDQwEH","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_0